\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Isotropic turbulence, spatially disjoint evaluation region ($1.95$M points, two velocity channels observed at 1\% of points, $K{=}8$, all 50 held-out snapshots). Spread--error and coverage ideals are 1.0 and 0.90. Senseiver is deterministic (CRPS reduces to MAE, no spread). Gen4Turb is retrained under our observation protocol at its native $120^3$; under its native shared-mask protocol, which observes all four channels (twice the information), it reaches 0.354/0.204 on an 8-snapshot subset. {\color  {red}[TODO: SiT-point and CoNFiLD rows: training/pipeline running.]}\relax }}{7}{table.caption.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:jhu}{{1}{7}{Isotropic turbulence, spatially disjoint evaluation region ($1.95$M points, two velocity channels observed at 1\% of points, $K{=}8$, all 50 held-out snapshots). Spread--error and coverage ideals are 1.0 and 0.90. Senseiver is deterministic (CRPS reduces to MAE, no spread). Gen4Turb is retrained under our observation protocol at its native $120^3$; under its native shared-mask protocol, which observes all four channels (twice the information), it reaches 0.354/0.204 on an 8-snapshot subset. \todo {SiT-point and CoNFiLD rows: training/pipeline running.}\relax }{table.caption.10}{}}
